  (text "J2 MUSIC MODULE INTERFACE - 24-pad 0.100in dual-sided gold-finger card edge (module carries the socket)\nPin numbers follow the bell-unit edge mated by EDAC 395-024-559-212 on merrie-minstrel-choir J2.\nOdd pins on one face, even pins on the other: confirm face and pin-1 orientation against a real module before layout.\nModule outputs bell data on 3,5,7,19,21,23 (BELL1-6) and 4,6,8,20,22,24 (BELL7-12).  Pin 9 = GND, pin 10 = module VCC (5V).\nPins 1,2,11-18: function unknown - each goes through TXS0108E to an ESP32 GPIO; DNP 0603 bypass R9-R18 across each.\nTranslator channels/GPIOs are assigned by board geometry (U5 = fingers 1-8, U6 = 11-18, U7 = 19-24).\n\nGPIO MAP  BELL1 IO7  BELL2 IO16  BELL3 IO18  BELL4 IO48  BELL5 IO36  BELL6 IO38  BELL7 IO15  BELL8 IO17  BELL9 IO8\n          BELL10 IO35  BELL11 IO37  BELL12 IO39   P1 IO5  P2 IO6  P11 IO9  P12 IO10  P13 IO11  P14 IO12  P15 IO13\n          P16 IO14  P17 IO21  P18 IO47   LVL_OE IO4  MOD_PWR_EN IO40  LED IO41  PLAY IO42  BOOT IO0  (N8 only: IO35-37 used)\n\nBOOT-SAFE DEFAULTS\n- LVL_OE pulled low by R6: translators are high-Z until firmware enables them.\n- MOD_PWR_EN pulled low by R8: module power (Q1 high-side switch) is off until firmware enables it.\n  Firmware sequence: drive LVL_OE low -> enable MOD_5V -> wait -> drive LVL_OE high.\n- Strapping pins IO0/IO3/IO45/IO46 are kept off the translator lines. IO1/IO2 are spare.\n- TXS0108E VCCB is on unswitched +5V so VCCA (3V3) is never above VCCB."
    (at 152.4 289.56 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid "e0f2bf57-bb43-49bb-b317-36270a62d171")
  )
